  "question": "After PROV-DEFECT-017 corrected issue 11 to ISBN 9787209115001, do public Google Books, Open Library or Internet Archive routes expose a bibliographic object, preview or full text that changes the 12IC full-text boundary?",
  "answer": "No new positive public object was recovered, but the route statuses must be distinguished precisely. Google Books API requests for the corrected ISBN and title were HTTP 429 rate-limited, so Google Books is RATE_LIMITED_UNRESOLVED rather than a zero-hit result. Open Library's exact corrected-ISBN endpoint returned HTTP 404 and its ISBN/title searches returned numFound=0. Internet Archive returned numFound=0 for corrected ISBN, quoted corrected ISBN and exact phrase 《国学季刊 第十一期》; its broader 国学季刊 AND 第十一期 query returned 151 unrelated/noisy objects, and the exact target-article-title query again returned the previously adjudicated unrelated identifier 3_20260926_202609. No full text was retrieved. Thus the 12IC public-fulltext boundary remains substantively intact after the ISBN correction, while its Google Books route must be superseded by a rate-limit access boundary rather than a no-candidate claim.",
